From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tsuji Riya <tsuji.riya@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:14:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/28] clk: Add Celestial CNC1800L clock driver

Describe the display PLL (TVE PLL, 27MHz * (fb + 1) / m with the
settings of the vendor disp_pll_cfg[] table) with the display and HDMI
TMDS dividers, and the clock enables of the display, TMDS, audio, CEC
and the USB PHY bypass ("enable and 48MHz"). Dividers and gates use the
generic clk-divider and clk-gate. Every clock output is enabled at
probe, as the vendor SDIO probe does, since the one the SDIO host needs
is not known.

Signed-off-by: Tsuji Riya <tsuji.riya@gmail.com>
---
 MAINTAINERS                |   2 +
 drivers/clk/Kconfig        |  10 ++
 drivers/clk/Makefile       |   1 +
 drivers/clk/clk-cnc1800l.c | 206 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 219 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/clk/clk-cnc1800l.c

